In this phase, the actual application is developed.

HTML Development

HTML is used to create the webpage structure, including:

Category selection
Budget input
Priority selection
Recommendation button
Recommendation area
Money-saving tips section
CSS Development

CSS is used to:

Design cards and panels.
Set fonts and spacing.
Create responsive layouts.
Style buttons and input fields.
Display the budget bar.
JavaScript Development

JavaScript performs the main application functions.

The recommendation system:

Reads the user's category.
Reads the budget.
Reads the selected priority.
Calculates the available budget.
Filters affordable items.
Scores the available items.
Selects a suitable recommendation.
Calculates remaining money.
Displays the result.
